WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.960
June 2014.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.200
Aerial cameras capture a riverbed in South
Texas.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:10.920
Nothing unusual.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:18.330
But when the same river is photographed the
following day, something appears in the mud.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.850
These spots are very out of place.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.200
Like they don't belong there.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.310
They could almost be like really large
footprints.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.620
They're huge.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.180
These are the footprints of a monster.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.770
Zoologist Roland Kays studies the image.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.930
He believes that the beast that left these
prints walks on two legs.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:46.840
Based on the pattern, it looks like they're
created by a bipedal creature, but it's got

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.640
to be something way bigger than a human.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:55.320
It's possible that these footprints are
actually maybe bears standing up on hind legs

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.370
or something like that.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:02.760
But even the biggest black bears create
prints just nine inches long, too small to be

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:03.990
seen from space.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.840
So the question is what caused them?

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:08.950
What left them there?

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:18.390
The image comes to the attention of Wildlife
Tracker Baltimore Galvan.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:28.090
Galvan analyzes the footprint in the picture
in an effort to reconstruct the scene.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:32.650
It looks like it was actually coming out of
the foliage right through here.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:37.720
And he probably saw something around this
area right up here.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:43.300
The shape and pattern of the footprints are
unlike anything he has come across.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:46.280
It raises a lot of questions.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:51.590
He's walking forward like this and then all
of a sudden from here, he just starts picking

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:54.050
up speed like it's actually running.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:56.240
It's very, very fascinating.

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:02.720
But there's only so much information to be
gleaned from the image.

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:08.080
I have to go down over there and just check
it out for myself.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.960
If I misidentify something.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.310
Then my reputation is gone.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:24.730
He and his partner had 400 miles to the
stretch of the Blanco River, which is

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:26.050
captured in the image.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:35.200
In the area. There have been several reports
of strange sounds and sightings of unusual

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:40.520
creatures. Galvan stops off to speak to some
witnesses.

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:43.910
Tell me exactly what you heard.

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:45.560
It was a weird sound.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.310
I'd say it was about nine foot tall, and it
was all hairy.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:50.940
It was covered in hair.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.030
There was nothing that wasn't hair.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:55.370
I did not see the face.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:56.030
We had to bend.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:58.130
Another another couple of feet taller than
me.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:02:59.720
Well, and.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:00.980
I'm kind of like, spellbound.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:02.090
What the heck was that?

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:08.490
Could reported sightings like these have
anything to do with the giant footprints in

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:09.690
the satellite image?

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:18.760
The animal described in the reports does
resemble a large beast known to have existed.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:23.680
This thing sounds like a creature called
gigantic Pythias, which was actually real.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.060
This thing was ten feet tall.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:28.000
It weighed £1,200 and it was related to
orangutans.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:31.390
It's the largest ape that scientists know
about.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:38.110
So just imagine, like a giant orangutan
wandering around the earth.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:46.570
But scientists believe gigantic epidemics
died out thousands of years ago.

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:53.110
When it comes to the pictures, it's always
blurry or difficult to see.

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:55.660
So the concrete evidence is not there.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.600
People have been looking for Bigfoot for
decades.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:05.590
If we haven't found incontrovertible
evidence yet, does it really exist?

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:14.210
Matching the satellite image with his GPS.

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:17.810
Galvan finds the section of river where the
prints were captured.

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:21.600
The footprint should be right up ahead.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.370
And this as far as we can go with the
vehicle.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:26.660
Right? Blanco.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:38.710
This stretch of river is isolated and rocky.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:44.650
The prints are not at all what Galvan was
expecting.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:49.120
Well, this is amazing.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:51.830
Breathtaking.

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:03.510
Galvin's monster hunt takes a strange turn.

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:12.920
They're not fresh at all.

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:17.330
These tracks have been here for a very, very
long time.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:18.770
For a very long time.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:22.880
This animal is way bigger than I expected.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:30.570
This one here, It's like five feet long and
four foot across.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:39.580
Up close, Galvan realizes this is no two
legged beast.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:42.370
This monster walks on four legs.

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:44.660
The prints are gigantic.

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:47.530
This thing is immensely big and heavy.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:52.610
I don't know the species of the animal that
made these tracks, but all that I know is a

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:53.690
huge animal.

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:57.810
Many times bigger than the biggest elephant.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:02.810
There is only one kind of creature that
could possibly leave footprints like this.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.900
This is another mystery that we have here.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:19.890
I don't know what kind of dinosaur made
these tracks.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.590
All that I know is a huge animal.

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:29.240
So what have we got here?

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:33.230
Photographs are sent to a team of experts
for analysis.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.410
So how long is one of these a given track
here?

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:40.370
They're about three feet across and about
three feet long.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:46.970
Examination of the animal's gait, the size
of the prints and the shape of the feet leads

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:48.710
the scientists to an extraordinary
conclusion.

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:52.010
These are sauropod tracks.

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:58.590
Sauropods were the largest dinosaurs ever to
have roamed the earth.

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:06.120
This monster herbivore was 100 feet long,
stood 60 feet high with a neck six times

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.620
longer than a giraffes.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.710
It weighed over 60 tons.

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:15.000
Can you imagine a herd of these thundering
through your neighborhood?

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:19.620
Even though there are gigantic, they were
actually vegetarians.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:24.260
They walk together in groups roaming around
in Texas.

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:30.470
Further analysis of the riverbed reveals over
90 individual tracks.

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:36.410
You could imagine them coming down to this
riverbed perhaps to get something to drink.

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:41.890
Sauropods were so massive.

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:48.510
Only the mighty T-Rex dared to take them on
an ambush predator.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:52.840
The T-Rex would choose locations like
riverbanks to mount an attack.

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:56.890
This herd of dinosaurs wouldn't have been
alone.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:00.370
There would have been predators hiding in
the bushes and trees.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:11.740
The team studies the local geology to guess
when these prints might have been made.

00:08:12.980 --> 00:08:17.510
The geology on it shows that they are about
100 million years old.

